        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(discord): notify agents of voice participant changes",
        "body": "Closes #106882\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nDiscord voice agents joined a channel without receiving an authoritative participant roster, and later joins, leaves, or moves were not delivered into the agent session. This left the agent unable to answer basic questions about who was present even though Discord already exposed voice-state events to the gateway.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe Discord gateway now maintains the current voice roster and injects silent, keyed system events into the routed supervisor session when a voice session starts or membership changes. Events include the bounded current roster, refresh after reconnect, ignore mute/deaf-only updates, and treat participant labels as untrusted text; no new Discord permission or config is required because voice mode already enables the `GuildVoiceStates` intent.\n\nThe shared system-event queue gains keyed replacement semantics so rapid roster churn coalesces without evicting unrelated events. AI-assisted implementation; reviewed against the complete branch diff.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAn agent entering Discord voice now knows who is already present. It stays informed when participants join, leave, or move, without speaking an unsolicited response merely because membership changed.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Live maintainer Discord session: gateway reached ready state, joined the configured voice channel, queued an initial four-participant roster, then queued one participant-joined and two participant-left events.\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxf7k568jhjzjebkmeq8wbty` ([run 29301395156](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29301395156)): 260 focused current-head tests passed across Discord gateway/provider/voice manager, system-event queue, and SDK baseline surfaces.\n- Patch-identical pre-rebase Testbox `tbx_01kxf6116vktv4ba229js6nngv`: touched-file lint passed with 0 warnings/errors; full production build passed.\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxf6j76d5dzx10kq8pjt2xj1` ([run 29300653355](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29300653355)): refreshed `pnpm check:changed` passed against current `main`, including typechecks, SDK API/surface guards, formatting, dependency guards, full core/extension lint, and architecture guards.\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxf7t52qhgpz2va5kaf8z5d9` ([run 29301546392](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29301546392)): the exact failed CI paths now pass (`pnpm deadcode:exports`, `pnpm check:architecture`) and the 260 focused tests pass after the fixup.\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD`\n\nNo screenshot is applicable: this changes agent-session context and gateway behavior, not a visual UI.\n",
